# SMART PLANT MONITORING SYSTEM

## 📌 Project Description

The **Smart Plant Monitoring System** is an IoT-based project designed to monitor plant and environmental conditions in real time. 
The system uses sensors to measure **soil moisture, temperature, humidity, and light intensity** and automatically controls devices
such as a **water pump and light** based on predefined conditions.

The collected data can be monitored remotely through a **web/mobile IoT platform**, allowing users to take care of plants efficiently from anywhere.

## 🚀 Features

* 💧 Real-time soil moisture monitoring
* 🌡️ Temperature monitoring
* 💦 Humidity monitoring
* ☀️ Light intensity detection using an LDR
* 🚰 Automatic water pump control
* 💡 Automatic light control based on sunlight
* 📱 Remote monitoring through Wi-Fi
* 🔔 Alerts for unsuitable plant conditions
* 🖥️ LCD display for real-time sensor values

## ⚙️ Working Principle

The sensors continuously collect data from the plant environment.

* If **soil moisture is below 30%**, the soil is considered dry and the **water pump turns ON**.
* Between **40% and 70%**, the soil condition is considered optimal.
* If soil moisture is **above 80%**, the soil is too wet and the **water pump remains OFF**.
* If the **temperature is below 18°C**, an alert is sent to the user.
* If the **temperature rises above 30°C**, the system can activate the pump based on the programmed conditions.
* The **LDR sensor** detects sunlight intensity and can automatically control a light when required.

